Based on the notes you provided, here is a structured summary and expansion of the **GatedDeltaNet** mechanism. This model appears to be a hybrid approach combining the efficiency of a Gated Diffusion Model (GDM) with the memory preservation capabilities of a Transformer.

### 1. Core Architecture Overview
The GatedDeltaNet operates on a **value head** (which acts as the primary memory source) and a **key-value pair head** (which acts as the prediction source).

*   **Recurrence vs. Cache**: Unlike standard Gated Diffusion Models (GDM) which use a key-value cache to store the entire history of the value head, GatedDeltaNet uses a **recurrent state** per value head. This allows the model to retain memory of the value head's evolution over time without storing the full history in a cache.
